Fixup for [PATCH v10 07/10] drm/xe/pm: Introduce xe_device_suspend/resume()

Apply on top of the full v10 series:

    patch -p1 -F3 < xe-flr-v11-fixup.diff
      or
    git apply --recount xe-flr-v11-fixup.diff

Two logical changes, kept in one file for convenience. For posting upstream
they should be split: hunk 1 is an independent fix to existing GuC submit
code and belongs before the series; hunks 2-4 are a fixup to patches 4 and 7.

1. xe_guc_submit.c
   Don't force the GT-reset path for a kernel queue that has been
   deliberately killed. During FLR teardown xe_guc_submit_pause_abort()
   kills every queue including the migrate queue, but the TDR then hits
   timeout_needs_gt_reset(), which is unconditionally true for
   EXEC_QUEUE_FLAG_KERNEL. xe_sched_invalidate_job(job, 2) is false on the
   first pass, so it calls xe_gt_reset_async() and returns via 'rearm'
   without ever reaching xe_sched_job_set_error(). That reset is itself a
   no-op, because uc_flr_prepare() already set guc->submission_state.stopped
   and the atomic_fetch_or() in guc_submit_reset_prepare() returns 1.
   Result: pending kernel-queue fences stay unsignalled across teardown.
   With this change a killed kernel queue falls through to the normal
   cancellation path and every pending job is completed with -ECANCELED.
   Behaviour outside teardown is unchanged, since kernel queues are only
   killed from deliberate teardown paths.

2. xe_device.c
   Don't drop dma mappings of pinned external bos during FLR prepare.
   xe_bo_pci_dev_remove_pinned() is a pci_device *removal* helper; FLR
   resets the state of the PCI function, not the IOMMU domain it is
   attached to, so those mappings stay valid across the reset. The call is
   also unpaired: the resume side takes the flr == true branch, which only
   calls xe_bo_restore_map() and never touches xe->pinned.late.external.
   xe_bo_restore_late() could not pair with it either, since
   xe_bo_restore_pinned() returns early without a backup object and FLR
   deliberately skips xe_bo_evict_all(). Removing it also drops the
   uninterruptible, untimed dma_fence_wait() that xe_tile_migrate_wait()
   performs after xe_irq_suspend().

3. xe_bo_evict.[ch]
   Revert the export added in patch 4, now that xe_bo_pci_dev_remove_all()
   is once again the only caller.

